[10.059552292,"o","\u001b[J\u001b[28;40r\u001b[28;1H\u001bM\u001bM\u001bM\u001bM\u001bM\u001bM\u001bM\u001bM\u001b[r\u001b[1;35r\u001b[27;1H\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  The pipe changed that. Introduced into Unix around 1973, it allowed the output of one process to become the input of\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  another process directly. The now-familiar vertical bar syntax, as in \u001b[38;5;6;49mwho | sort | lpr\u001b[39;49m, made this idea compact and\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  expressive. A user could take a stream of text, filter it, transform it, sort it, count it, or send it elsewhere\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  without creating temporary files. This was not just a convenience; it reshaped the way Unix programs were designed.\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  Ken Thompson implemented pipes in Unix after McIlroy’s proposal. The implementation fit naturally with Unix’s\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  “everything is a file” philosophy. A pipe looked much like a file descriptor to a program, so existing tools could\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  often participate in p"]
[10.066328959,"o","ipelines without special knowledge of pipes. Programs simply read from standard input and wrote\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  to standard output. This encouraged a style of programming based on text streams, composability, and minimal\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  assumptions about where data came from or where it would go.\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b[r\u001b[36;3H\u001b[36;2H\u001b[0m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\u001b[37;2H\u001b[0m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\u001b[38;36H\u001b[0m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\u001b[39;2H\u001b[0m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\u001b[40;44H\u001b[0m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[1m›\u001b[38;3H\u001b[22m\u001b[2m\u001b[2mRun /review on my current changes\u001b[40;3H\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;246;226;183;49mgpt-5.5 medium\u001b[2m\u001b[39;49m · \u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;171;223;167;49m/private/tmp/rt3-capture\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b[0 q\u001b[?25h\u001b[38;3H\u001b[?2026l\u001b[?2026h\u001b[36;2H\u001b[0m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\u001b[37;2H\u001b[0m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\u001b[38;36H\u001b[0m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\u001b[39;2H\u001b[0m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\u001b[40;44H\u001b[0m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b[0 q\u001b[?25h\u001b[38;3H\u001b[?2026l"]
